{
  "esm": "1.3.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "mom6_ppm_face_integral",
    "description": "The MOM6 PPM layer-flux integral at one cell face (zonal_flux_layer, MOM_continuity_PPM.F90:933-956, VOL_CFL=False), ONE law for both axes and both flow directions: flux = dy*u*(h_face + CFL*(0.5*(h_back - h_face) + curv_3*(CFL - 1.5))) with CFL = |u|*dt*I_dx (the upwind-cell Courant number) and curv_3 = (h_face + h_back) - 2*h_0, and flux = 0 for u == 0 (the Fortran's else branch, F90:953-955). The caller selects the UPWIND cell: for u > 0 the upwind cell is the cell itself (h_face = its east edge, h_back = its west edge, h_0 = its thickness, I_dx = its 1/dxT, the F90:933-939 branch: uh = dy*u*(h_E(i) + CFL*(0.5*(h_W(i) - h_E(i)) + curv_3*(CFL - 1.5)))); for u < 0 the upwind cell is the east/north neighbor (h_face = its west/south edge, h_back = its east/north edge, h_0 = its thickness, I_dx = its 1/dxT, the F90:940-949 branch: uh = dy*u*(h_W(i+1) + CFL*(0.5*(h_E(i+1) - h_W(i+1)) + curv_3*(CFL - 1.5)))); the two Fortran branches are the same parabola integral with the two edge roles swapped, which is why one law serves both. The edges h_face/h_back are the PPM_limit_pos-limited edges of the upwind cell (mom6_ppm_limited_edge), the face length dy is dy_Cu (zonal) or dx_Cv (meridional), and the flux is the layer volume flux [m3 s-1]. Pure scalar algebra; no branch inside the law beyond the zero-velocity floor, so the sign selection lives at the rule call site.",
    "license": "MIT",
    "tags": ["esd:stencil", "family:mom6_cgrid", "grid:mom6_cgrid", "op:flux"],
    "references": [
      {
        "citation": "Colella, P., & Woodward, P. R. (1984). The Piecewise Parabolic Method (PPM) for gas-dynamical simulations. Journal of Computational Physics, 54(1), 174-201. (The parabolic face integral.)",
        "doi": "10.1016/0021-9991(84)90143-8"
      }
    ]
  },
  "expression_templates": {
    "mom6_ppm_face_integral": {
      "params": ["u", "dt", "dy", "I_dx", "h_face", "h_back", "h_0"],
      "description": "The MOM6 PPM layer-flux integral at one face (MOM_continuity_PPM.F90:933-956)",
      "body": {
        "op": "ifelse",
        "args": [
          { "op": "==", "args": ["u", 0.0] },
          0.0,
          {
            "op": "*",
            "args": [
              "dy",
              {
                "op": "*",
                "args": [
                  "u",
                  {
                    "op": "+",
                    "args": [
                      "h_face",
                      {
                        "op": "*",
                        "args": [
                          { "op": "*", "args": [{ "op": "abs", "args": ["u"] }, { "op": "*", "args": ["dt", "I_dx"] }] },
                          {
                            "op": "+",
                            "args": [
                              {
                                "op": "*",
                                "args": [
                                  0.5,
                                  { "op": "-", "args": ["h_back", "h_face"] }
                                ]
                              },
                              {
                                "op": "*",
                                "args": [
                                  {
                                    "op": "-",
                                    "args": [
                                      { "op": "+", "args": ["h_face", "h_back"] },
                                      { "op": "*", "args": [2.0, "h_0"] }
                                    ]
                                  },
                                  {
                                    "op": "-",
                                    "args": [
                                      { "op": "*", "args": [{ "op": "abs", "args": ["u"] }, { "op": "*", "args": ["dt", "I_dx"] }] },
                                      1.5
                                    ]
                                  }
                                ]
                              }
                            ]
                          }
                        ]
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      }
    }
  }
}
